@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho

title GOV-1 — Integrated Control Case Traceability

rectangle "User Story / Context of Use" as US
rectangle "Requirement" as REQ
rectangle "Risk" as RISK
rectangle "Control Obligation" as CTRL
rectangle "Implementation Mechanism" as IMPL
rectangle "Verification Evidence / Receipt" as EVID
rectangle "Control Assessment" as ASSESS
rectangle "Residual / Nonconformance" as NC
rectangle "CAPA / Bounded Repair" as CAPA
rectangle "Service Change State" as CHANGE
rectangle "Release / Observation" as RELEASE

US --> REQ : derives
REQ --> RISK : threat / failure modes
RISK --> CTRL : treatment
CTRL --> IMPL : implemented by
IMPL --> EVID : verified by
EVID --> ASSESS : evaluate exact scope
ASSESS --> RELEASE : satisfied / accepted
ASSESS --> NC : partial / failed / insufficient
NC --> CAPA : corrective / preventive action
CAPA --> CHANGE : proposed -> implemented
CHANGE --> EVID : verify / validate
RELEASE --> RISK : continual improvement / observed incidents

note left of ASSESS
  Statuses:
  satisfied
  not_satisfied
  insufficient_evidence
  not_applicable
end note

note right of EVID
  Evidence state is separate from change state:
  source_written
  compile_checked
  fixture_checked
  runtime_observed
  production_observed
end note

note bottom of CTRL
  Standards are provenance/control lenses,
  not an automatic certification claim.
end note
@enduml
